# ax release & install

## Build output path

Cargo uses `target-dev/` (see `.cargo/config.toml`), **not** `target/debug/`. Never test CLI changes with `.\target\debug\ax.exe`.

After any `crates/ax-cli/` change: run `.\scripts\reinstall-cli.ps1` and **verify all ax.exe copies are identical** before handoff (see below).

**Command Center web UI (`crates/ax-web/web-ui/`):** `ax web` embeds `web-ui/dist` at **compile time**. `npm run build` alone does **not** update localhost:7070. After any web-ui change, run:

```powershell
.\scripts\rebuild-web.ps1
```

This rebuilds `ax-cli` (cargo runs `npm run build` via `ax-web/build.rs`), syncs all three `ax.exe` copies, restarts `ax web`, and verifies the served JS bundle matches `dist/index.html`. Never hand off web-ui work without this check.

**Local release (no GitHub):** `.\scripts\ship-local.ps1` then `ax upgrade --local`.

## Multi-location binary sync (ALWAYS check)

Windows installs ax in **three** places. Prefer `.\scripts\release-local.ps1` / `reinstall-cli.ps1` — they **copy** `target-dev\release\ax.exe` to all three paths (with rename-away unlock). Do **not** rely on `cargo install` alone: it rebuilds for minutes, Cursor MCP often respawns `ax.exe`, and replace fails with **Access is denied**.

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `%USERPROFILE%\.cargo\bin\ax.exe` | PATH / MCP fallback |
| `%LOCALAPPDATA%\ax\current\bin\ax.exe` | Cursor MCP config target |
| `%LOCALAPPDATA%\ax\current\ax.exe` | Legacy installer root (easy to miss) |

**After every build/reinstall**, confirm all three match `target-dev\release\ax.exe` (hash + size + timestamp):

```powershell
$src = "target-dev\release\ax.exe"
$targets = @(
  "$env:USERPROFILE\.cargo\bin\ax.exe",
  "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\ax\current\bin\ax.exe",
  "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\ax\current\ax.exe"
)
$hash = (Get-FileHash $src).Hash
foreach ($t in $targets) {
  if (-not (Test-Path $t)) { Write-Warning "missing: $t"; continue }
  $h = (Get-FileHash $t).Hash
  if ($h -ne $hash) { throw "STALE: $t (hash mismatch — copy from $src)" }
}
Write-Host "OK: all ax.exe copies match $hash"
(Get-Command ax).Source
ax --version
```

If any path is stale: kill all `ax.exe`, copy `$src` to every target, re-run the check. `.\scripts\release-local.ps1` syncs all three automatically; still verify before handoff.

**Never** mark ax-cli / Command Center work complete without this check passing or an explicit blocked reason.

## Version bumps

Use `.\scripts\release-tag.ps1 -Bump patch|minor|major`:

| Bump | Example |
|------|---------|
| patch | 2.0.14 → 2.0.15 |
| minor | 2.0.14 → **2.1.0** (not 2.0.15) |
| major | 2.0.14 → 3.0.0 |

Never document or pin a version (`AX_VERSION`, docs, README) until the GitHub release tag exists with all six platform assets.

Current Command Center release: **v4.7.0**.

## Install / upgrade pitfalls

- **`AX_VERSION` env var** — if set (session, User, or profile), `install.ps1` / `install.sh` pin to that tag. Invalid pins now auto-fallback to latest and clear stale User env; still avoid documenting unreleased pins.
- **`ax ship`** — subcommand is `ax ship --watch`, not `ax ship watch`.
- **MCP** — restart ax MCP in Cursor after reinstall so agents use the new binary.

## Release checklist

1. Commit feature + docs
2. `.\scripts\release-tag.ps1 -Bump … -Force -Wait`
3. Align doc version strings with the actual tag (minor bump ≠ patch increment)
4. `.\scripts\deploy-netlify.ps1` if site/install scripts changed outside CI
5. Smoke: `ax --version`, `ax ship --help`, `irm …/install.ps1 | iex` without `AX_VERSION` set
